<title>GERMANY: German Unilever says Nordsee sale undecided.</title>
<headline>German Unilever says Nordsee sale undecided.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>A spokesman for the German subsidiary of Anglo-Dutch group Unilever said on Monday no decision had been taken on whether the group was to sell its Nordsee German fish business.</p>
<p>&quot;No decision has been taken. The question is being studied, but the timeframe for a decision is anything up to late March,&quot; a German Unilever spokesman said by telephone.</p>
<p>Britain's The Observer newspaper had reported on Sunday that a sale of the unit for around 200 million pounds ($326.4 million) was imminent and that several firms were interested in buying it.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
<p>($ = 0.612 British Pounds)</p>
